		<title>By: Elizabeth "Elsa" Weber-Fraley</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=703&#038;cpage=1#comment-6502</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Elizabeth "Elsa" Weber-Fraley]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 27 Nov 2010 17:13:50 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=703#comment-6502</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[In my family of origin, the arts were sadly devalued. Fortunately, Newell came along as the eloquent spokesperson for the Arts and replaced those erroneous tapes that were playing in my head.  He used to say, with so much courage and conviction, that a &quot;Life without the Arts is not worth living!!!&quot;  

And to this, I say, Amen! 

Thank you, Newell.
Elizabeth &quot;Elsa&quot; Weber]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>In my family of origin, the arts were sadly devalued. Fortunately, Newell came along as the eloquent spokesperson for the Arts and replaced those erroneous tapes that were playing in my head.  He used to say, with so much courage and conviction, that a &#8220;Life without the Arts is not worth living!!!&#8221;  </p>
<p>And to this, I say, Amen! </p>
<p>Thank you, Newell.<br />
Elizabeth &#8220;Elsa&#8221; Weber</p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
	<item>
		<title>By: Majida Gibson</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=703&#038;cpage=1#comment-4519</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Majida Gibson]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 09 May 2010 23:07:26 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=703#comment-4519</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Newell was a beloved friend, as well as an enduring director of the erstwhile Abode Choir...how we made him suffer! He had a sly sense of humor, a great love of music , as well as food. One lunch he made and served me spaghetti carbonera...full of butter, bacon and other forms of cholesterol! And we loved it! I miss him, and his loving companion Jack Hurley who has also passed.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Newell was a beloved friend, as well as an enduring director of the erstwhile Abode Choir&#8230;how we made him suffer! He had a sly sense of humor, a great love of music , as well as food. One lunch he made and served me spaghetti carbonera&#8230;full of butter, bacon and other forms of cholesterol! And we loved it! I miss him, and his loving companion Jack Hurley who has also passed.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
